---
pagination:
  data: legacyRedirects
  size: 1
  alias: r
  addAllPagesToCollections: false
permalink: "{{ r.from }}"
layout: null
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{%- comment -%}
  Old URLs from the first version of the site (rdjarbeng.github.io/RDjarbeng/...,
  which GitHub now forwards to rdjarbeng.com/RDjarbeng/...). GitHub Pages cannot
  send real 301s, so each old URL gets a page that redirects instantly; Google
  treats an immediate meta refresh like a permanent redirect. See
  _data/legacyRedirects.js for the list.
{%- endcomment -%}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Moved</title>
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ site.url }}{{ r.to }}">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
<meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ r.to }}">
<script>location.replace({{ r.to | jsonify }} + location.hash);</script>
</head>
<body>
<p>This page has moved to <a href="{{ r.to }}">{{ site.url }}{{ r.to }}</a>.</p>
</body>
</html>
